# CODEOWNERS for Binary_Defect_Repairing_Engine.
# GitHub uses the last matching pattern, so specific module rules come after
# the default. A second handle on a path is a review backup, not an edit
# permission. The module registry in modules.json is the source of truth.
#
# Every path lists M1 as a co-owner. A pull request author cannot approve their
# own PR, so a module whose only code owner is the author would be permanently
# blocked by "Require review from Code Owners". The co-owner is a review backup,
# not an edit permission: editing stays with the module owner as in modules.json.
